[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8331"] :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is a linear transformation" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37873"] :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} & =18{v}_{1}+3{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} \\\\  & =18({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =18(0)+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =3{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=T(3{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}) & =3T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37898"] :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74780/selection/611e98d4a597904ebb9b9ff7a6c27199ebc3901c179e4dfe439e8ad415985ec4" :answer/id #uuid "8e298117-c97c-5ee4-830a-04ccc3393618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-40 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 45\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74780/selection/026d42095f1e47728c71a3bfceb8ab398c18c291215f5d6866b7605adee39474" :answer/id #uuid "4715a94f-0da4-5045-820c-ca8b533f5932" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}64 \\\\ -32 \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74780/selection/15aedda650d4d03e7c97c70877a1dedcdca39f1a4b3d5669c040d669c0e4939b" :answer/id #uuid "9cbf06d8-b7ae-5735-85df-36c0a77670b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74780/selection/47db49b52461d828456df9b83f8616e2382903c15f64205c9160beb1ab81ee90" :answer/id #uuid "46d9cda0-53aa-595e-940b-2ee701c33df4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-64 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74780/selection/a7afdcd2b0d701fe2f1aa0a83732f8cde1ba612d1ed446c254280571fac165b3" :answer/id #uuid "873dab30-b0b1-5c58-a91a-b667ba08b91b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74780/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ac0d906-d18d-5aeb-8c3